            <ArticleTitle>Equianalgesic dosing: principles of practice for the care team.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>80-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1188/13.CJON.80-83</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Opioids are the basis for managing cancer-related pain. Pain assessment and management are critical competencies for the clinical care team to improve quality of life for patients with cancer. Knowledge and application of evidence-based practice approaches to cancer pain relief, including the principles of equianalgesic dosing, opioid switching and rotation, and use of coanalgesics, can lead to improved patient outcomes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
